    {
      "type": "grammar",
      "title": "Time words go before the verb",
      "body": "In Chinese, words that say when something happens, like 早上 or 中午, come before the verb, never at the end of the sentence as in English. Put the time word right after the person: 我 + time + verb. You can also start the sentence with the time word.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "zh": "我早上喝牛奶。",
          "en": "I drink milk in the morning."
        },
        {
          "zh": "他中午吃饺子。",
          "en": "He eats dumplings at noon."
        },
        {
          "zh": "上午我在家。",
          "en": "I'm at home in the morning."
        }
      ]
